<title>MOROCCO: Morocco's Cosumar raises profits.</title>
<headline>Morocco's Cosumar raises profits.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's leading sugar firm Cosumar, a subsidiary of ONA group, showed a net profits of 223.5 million dirhams ($24 million) in 1996, up from 155.6 million dirhams in the previous year.</p>
<p>Cosumar's turnover stood at 3.31 billion dirhams in 1996 against 3.45 billion dirhams in 1995.</p>
<p>Established in Casablanca in 1932, Cosumar has a production capacity of 600,000 tonnes annually.</p>
<p>One of the 47 stocks listed on the Casablanca stock exchange, it was last traded at 880 dirhams.</p>
</text>
